---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: projects/umbra/docs/index.html
title: umbra docs | Kai Siren
description: The documentation for umbra, a config driven occlusion framework. Install it and watch a refusal, then the guides, the reference, and the concepts underneath.
robots: follow, index
canonical: /projects/umbra/docs/
project: umbra
projectPage: /projects/umbra/
---
{#- The front door. umbra's own docs/index.md is the model the other three
    repos have nothing of, so this renders the same manifest the sidebar and
    the pager walk rather than restating it. -#}
<div class="docs docs--umbra">

  <nav class="docs__crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <ol>
      <li><a href="{{ projectPage }}">{{ project }}</a></li>
      <li aria-current="page">Docs</li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <div class="docs__col docs__front">
    <div class="docs__brand">
      <img src="/images/marks/umbra.png" alt="" width="220" height="220" decoding="async">
      <span>
        <b>umbra</b>
        <span class="docs__brand-sub">docs</span>
      </span>
    </div>
    <h1>Name every command, then prove it.</h1>
    <p class="docs__lede">
      umbra sits between semi-trusted automation and the host system. What you did not
      declare does not get through. Policy lives in a KDL guardfile rather than in code,
      enforced across two surfaces: subprocess execution and outbound HTTP.
    </p>
    <p class="docs__lede">
      If you are still deciding whether any of that is your problem, the
      <a href="{{ projectPage }}">case for umbra</a> is the better place to start. These
      pages assume you already decided.
    </p>

    <p class="docs__snapshot">
      Snapshot of <a href="{{ umbraDocs.source.docs }}" rel="noreferrer">umbra
      {{ umbraDocs.source.commit }}</a>, {{ umbraDocs.source.date }}. Copied by
      hand, so the repository is the source of truth if the two disagree.
    </p>

    <div class="docs__shelves">
      {%- for shelf in umbraDocs.shelves %}
      <section class="docs__shelf-block">
        <p class="docs__shelf">{{ shelf.title }}</p>
        <ul>
          {%- for page in shelf.pages %}
          <li>
            <a href="/projects/umbra/docs/{{ page.slug }}/">
              {{ page.title }}
              <span>{{ page.blurb }}</span>
            </a>
          </li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
      </section>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
